<title>DENMARK: Danish June current account surplus 1.2 bln DKK.</title>
<headline>Danish June current account surplus 1.2 bln DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's current account surplus fell to 1.2 billion crowns in June, from a revised 1.4 billion crown surplus in May, the national statistics office said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>DANISH CURRENT ACCOUNT (billions of crowns)</p>
<p>Figures for the past three, six and 12 month periods:</p>
<p>			 Three-month Six-month Twelve-month</p>
<p>Current account     4.5	    13.5	 10.6</p>
<p>Goods		  11.5	    22.2	 40.3</p>
<p>Services		2.5	     2.9	  5.2</p>
<p>Interest, other    -9.5	   -11.6	-34.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are subject to rounding. Market analysts polled by Reuters had predicted an average June current account surplus of 2.5 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969650</p>
</text>
